---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../../components/parts/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/parts/Footer.astro';
import { getLangFromUrl } from '../../i18n/utils';

const lang = getLangFromUrl(Astro.url);
---

<Layout 
  title="Privacy Policy - Benito González García" 
  description="Privacy policy and legal notice of Benito González García - Professional saxophonist" 
  lang={lang}
>
  <Header />
  
  <main class="pt-20 pb-16">
    <div class="container mx-auto px-4 max-w-4xl">
      <h1 class="text-8xl font-segmentA uppercase tracking-wide font-bold mb-8 text-primary">Legal Notice and Privacy Policy</h1>
      
        <h2 class="text-6xl font-segmentA uppercase tracking-wide font-bold mb-4 text-primary">1. Information</h2>
        <p class="mb-4">
          This website is owned by <strong>Benito González García</strong> (hereinafter, indistinctly,
          <strong>benitogonzalezsax</strong> or <strong>benitogonzalezsax.com</strong>).
        </p>
        <p class="mb-4">
          <strong>Tax ID (C.I.F.):</strong> 49440443-B<br />
          <strong>Address:</strong> Calle Andrés Ureña Román nº 57, 30870 Mazarrón (Murcia), Spain.<br />
          <strong>Contact email:</strong>
          <a href="mailto:info@benitogonzalezsax.com" class="text-primary underline">
            info@benitogonzalezsax.com
          </a>
        </p>
        <p class="mb-4">
          Through this statement, visitors and users of <strong>benitogonzalezsax.com</strong>
          (hereinafter, the <strong>WEBSITE</strong>) are informed of the policy our business follows regarding the
          processing of data received through this site. The purpose of our privacy policy is to comply as fully as
          possible with the current legislation on the protection of personal data. If you have any doubts about the
          confidentiality or the processing of your data, or if you wish to exercise any of your legally recognised
          rights of information, objection, rectification, erasure and portability (or any other right you consider may
          apply), you may contact:
        </p>
        <p class="mb-4">
          <strong>BENITOGONZALEZSAX</strong><br />
          Email:
          <a href="mailto:info@benitogonzalezsax.com" class="text-primary underline">
            info@benitogonzalezsax.com
          </a>
        </p>
        <p class="mb-4">
          All of the above is in compliance with Article 11 of Organic Law 3/2018 of 5 December on the Protection of
          Personal Data and guarantee of digital rights, as well as Articles 12 to 14 of Regulation (EU) 2016/679 of the
          European Parliament and of the Council of 27 April 2016 (hereinafter, the <strong>GDPR</strong>).
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-6xl font-segmentA uppercase tracking-wide font-bold mb-4 text-primary">2. Purpose of the data collected and consent to processing</h2>
        <p>
          In accordance with Article 14 of the GDPR, the <strong>USER</strong> is informed that, through contact or
          subscription forms, data are collected and stored in a file for the sole purpose of sending electronic
          communications, such as newsletters, new posts, commercial offers, as well as other communications that
          <strong>BENITOGONZALEZSAX</strong> considers to be of interest to its USERS.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-4">
          Fields marked as mandatory are essential in order to fulfil the stated purpose. Likewise, the data provided may
          be used to respond to the requests submitted by USERS.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-4">
          Only the owner will have access to your data and under no circumstances will these data be assigned, shared,
          transferred or sold to any third party.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-4">
          Acceptance of the privacy policy, by means of the established procedure, shall be understood, for all intents
          and purposes, as the provision of <strong>UNEQUIVOCAL CONSENT</strong> –within the meaning of Article 6 of
          Organic Law 3/2018 of 5 December on the Protection of Personal Data and guarantee of digital rights– by the
          USER for the processing of personal data under the terms set out in this document, as well as for the
          international transfer of data that may take place solely due to the physical location of the facilities of
          service providers and data processors.
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-4xl font-segmentA uppercase tracking-wide font-bold mb-4 text-primary">Data processed</h3>
        <h4 class="text-lg uppercase font-bold mb-2 text-primary">A. Professional data</h4>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-4">
          <li>Full name / trade name</li>
          <li>Project name</li>
          <li>Username and password</li>
          <li>Description of services</li>
          <li>Fees or rates</li>
          <li>Province and town/city of residence</li>
          <li>Provinces where you wish to work</li>
          <li>Photographs, videos, portfolio</li>
          <li>Phone number, email and social networks</li>
          <li>Ratings and reviews received</li>
        </ul>

        <h4 class="text-lg uppercase font-bold mb-2 text-primary">B. Client data</h4>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-4">
          <li>Full name (if registered manually)</li>
          <li>Email</li>
          <li>Phone number (optional)</li>
          <li>Username and password</li>
          <li>Data provided in reviews</li>
          <li>Data obtained through Google Sign-In (if used): name, email, photo</li>
        </ul>

        <h4 class="text-lg uppercase font-bold mb-4 text-primary">C. Browsing data</h4>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-4">
          <li>Technical, statistical or customization cookies</li>
          <li>IP address</li>
          <li>Access logs</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="text-lg uppercase font-bold mb-2 text-primary">3. Purposes of processing</h3>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-4">
          <li>Managing the registration of professionals and clients</li>
          <li>Enabling the publication and visibility of professional profiles</li>
          <li>Enabling the rating and review system, with public visibility</li>
          <li>Providing external contact tools between the parties</li>
          <li>Improving the security and operation of the Platform</li>
          <li>Compliance with legal obligations</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 class="text-lg uppercase font-bold mb-2 text-primary">4. Legal basis</h2>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-4">
          <li>Performance of a contract (Art. 6.1.b GDPR): registration and use of the service</li>
          <li>Consent (Art. 6.1.a GDPR): cookies, newsletters, multimedia data</li>
          <li>Legitimate interest (Art. 6.1.f GDPR): fraud prevention, assessment of professionals</li>
          <li>Legal obligation (Art. 6.1.c GDPR): retention of data, requests from authorities</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 class="text-lg uppercase font-bold mb-2 text-primary">5. Public nature of professional data</h2>
        <p>Professionals accept that:</p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-4">
          <li>Their contact details (phone, email, social networks) will be public and visible to clients.</li>
          <li>The reviews submitted by clients may be displayed on their profile.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 class="text-lg uppercase font-bold mb-2 text-primary">6. Data disclosures</h2>
        <p>No data are disclosed to third parties except in the following cases:</p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-4">
          <li>Technology providers (hosting, email, analytics), under GDPR-compliant data processing agreements.</li>
          <li>Legal requirements.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 class="text-lg uppercase font-bold mb-2 text-primary">7. Data retention</h2>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-4">
          <li>Active account: while the user maintains their registration.</li>
          <li>After account closure: data blocked for 5 years for legal liability purposes.</li>
          <li>Reviews: may be anonymised or deleted upon justified request.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 class="text-6xl font-segmentA uppercase tracking-wide font-bold mb-4 text-primary">3. Compliance with applicable regulations</h2>
        <p class="mb-4">
          The WEBSITE complies with the provisions of Organic Law 3/2018 of 5 December on the Protection of Personal Data
          and guarantee of digital rights, as well as Regulation (EU) 2016/679 (GDPR – General Data Protection
          Regulation) and any other regulations in force and applicable from time to time, ensuring the proper use and
          processing of users’ personal data.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-4">
          Likewise, the WEBSITE complies with Law 34/2002 of 11 July on Information Society Services and Electronic
          Commerce and will request the USER’s consent at all times for the processing of their email address for
          commercial purposes.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-4">
          In accordance with Organic Law 3/2018 of 5 December on the Protection of Personal Data and guarantee of digital
          rights, we inform you that the data provided, as well as those derived from your browsing, may be stored in the
          WEBSITE’s files and processed for the purpose of responding to your request and maintaining the relationship
          established through the forms you complete.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-4">
          Additionally, the USER consents to the processing of their data in order to be informed, by any means,
          including email, about products and services of the WEBSITE.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-4">
          If the USER does not authorise the processing of their data for the aforementioned purpose, they may exercise
          their right to object to the processing of their data under the terms and conditions set out below in the
          section “Exercise of ARCO-P rights”, in accordance with Article 12 et seq. of Organic Law 3/2018 of 5 December
          on the Protection of Personal Data and guarantee of digital rights.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-6xl font-segmentA uppercase tracking-wide font-bold mb-4 text-primary">4. Security measures</h2>
        <p class="mb-4">
          <strong>BENITOGONZALEZSAX</strong> informs you that it has implemented the necessary technical and
          organisational security measures to ensure the security of your personal data and to prevent their alteration,
          loss, unauthorised processing or access, taking into account the state of technology, the nature of the data
          stored and the risks to which they are exposed, whether arising from human action or from the physical or
          natural environment. All of this is in accordance with Articles 28 et seq. of Organic Law 3/2018 of 5 December
          on the Protection of Personal Data and guarantee of digital rights and Article 32 of the GDPR.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-4">
          Likewise, <strong>BENITOGONZALEZSAX</strong> has established additional measures to reinforce the
          confidentiality and integrity of the information within its organisation, continuously monitoring, supervising
          and evaluating processes to ensure respect for data privacy.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-6xl font-segmentA uppercase tracking-wide font-bold mb-4 text-primary">5. Exercise of ARCO-P rights: access, rectification, cancellation, objection and portability</h2>
        <div class="flex flex-col gap-4 mb-4">

          <p>
            Any natural persons who have provided their data through the WEBSITE may contact the owner in order to
            exercise, free of charge, their rights of access, rectification, erasure, objection and portability in
            relation to the data stored in its files, in accordance with Article 12 et seq. of Organic Law 3/2018 of 5
            December on the Protection of Personal Data and guarantee of digital rights.
          </p>
          <p>
            The quickest and simplest way is to log into your user account directly and update your data or delete your
            user account. Any information that we are required to retain on the basis of a legal or contractual
            obligation will be blocked and used solely for such purposes instead of being deleted.
          </p>
          <p>
            Data subjects may exercise their rights by sending a written communication to
            <strong> BENITOGONZALEZSAX</strong> with the reference “Data protection”, specifying their details,
            proving their identity and stating the grounds for their request at the following address:
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>BENITOGONZALEZSAX</strong><br />
            Address: Calle Andrés Ureña Román nº 57, 30870 Mazarrón (Murcia), Spain.
          </p>
          <p>
            They may also exercise their ARCO-P rights by sending an email to:
            <a href="mailto:leadslend@gmail.com" class="text-primary underline">
              leadslend@gmail.com
            </a>
          </p>
        </div>

        <h2 class="text-6xl font-segmentA uppercase tracking-wide font-bold mb-4 text-primary">6. External links</h2>
        <div class="flex flex-col gap-4 mb-4">
          <p>
            As a service to our visitors, our WEBSITE may include hyperlinks to other sites that are not operated or
            controlled by the WEBSITE. Therefore, <strong>LEADSLEND</strong> does not guarantee and is not responsible
            for the lawfulness, reliability, usefulness, truthfulness or timeliness of the content of such websites or of
            their privacy practices.
          </p>
          <p>
            Please, before providing your personal information on these websites that are external to
            <strong> BENITOGONZALEZSAX</strong>, bear in mind that their privacy practices may differ from ours.
          </p>
          <p>
            The sole purpose of these links is to provide the USER with the possibility of accessing such links and
            learning about our work, although the WEBSITE does not offer or market, either by itself or through third
            parties, the information, content and services available on the linked sites, nor does it approve, supervise
            or control in any way the content and services or any material of any nature contained therein.
            <strong> BENITOGONZALEZSAX</strong> shall not be responsible in any case for any results that may arise for
            the USER as a result of accessing such links.
          </p>
        </div>

        <h2 class="text-6xl font-segmentA uppercase tracking-wide font-bold mb-4 text-primary">7. Changes to the privacy policy</h2>
        <div class="flex flex-col gap-4 mb-4">
          <p>
            <strong>BENITOGONZALEZSAX</strong> reserves the right to modify its Privacy Policy, at its own discretion or
            due to a legislative, case law or doctrinal change by the Spanish Data Protection Agency.
          </p>
          <p>
            Any modification to the Privacy Policy will be published at least ten days before its effective application.
            The use of the WEBSITE after such changes implies acceptance of them.
          </p>
        </div>

        <h2 class="text-6xl font-segmentA uppercase tracking-wide font-bold mb-4 text-primary">8. Data controller and data processors</h2>
        <div class="flex flex-col gap-4 mb-4">
          <p>
            The data controller is BENITOGONZALEZSAX.
          </p>
          <p>
            As data processors external to the aforementioned controller:
            <strong>BENITOGONZALEZSAX</strong> has contracted hosting services from FIREBASE GOOGLE IRELAND LIMITED, a
            company established and operating under the laws of Ireland
          <p>
            (registration number: 368047 / VAT number: IE6388047V)<br/>
            Gordon House, Barrow Street, Dublin 4, Ireland. 
          </p>
          <p>
            Privacy policy of tracking tools used on this site: Google (Analytics).
          </p>
          <p>
            On the WEBSITE, we also analyse our users’ preferences, demographic characteristics, traffic patterns and
            other information on an aggregate basis in order to better understand who constitutes our audience and what
            they need. Tracking our users’ preferences also helps us show you the most relevant advertisements.
          </p>
          <p>
            The user and, in general, any natural or legal person may establish a hyperlink or technical link device (for
            example, links or buttons) from their website to the WEBSITE (the “Hyperlink”). The establishment of the
            Hyperlink does not in any case imply the existence of any relationship between the WEBSITE and the owner of
            the site or web page on which the Hyperlink is established, nor the acceptance or approval by the WEBSITE of
            its contents or services. In any case, the WEBSITE reserves the right to prohibit or disable at any time any
            Hyperlink to the WEBSITE.
          </p>
        </div>
        

        <h2 class="text-6xl font-segmentA uppercase tracking-wide font-bold mb-4 text-primary">9. Do you not wish to receive information from us or do you wish to withdraw your consent?</h2>
        <div class="flex flex-col gap-4 mb-4">
          <p>
            In accordance with Law 34/2002 of 11 June on Information Society Services and Electronic Commerce, you may
            object to the use of your information for advertising purposes, market research or the development of
            satisfaction surveys at any time, as well as withdraw your consent at any time (with no retroactive effect).
          </p>
          <p>
            To do so, you must send an email to:
            <a href="mailto:leadslend@gmail.com" class="text-primary underline">
              leadslend@gmail.com
            </a>
          </p>
          <p>
            If you have received advertising by email, you may also object directly from that email by clicking on the
            link included therein and following the instructions provided. Another simpler way is to access your user
            account and select the appropriate options.
          </p>
          <p>
            Please note that our systems may require a period of time, which in no case will exceed 48 hours, for your
            objection or revocation to become fully effective, during which time you may still receive messages.
          </p>
          <p>
            With regard to the management of your data associated with the social media profiles of
            <strong> BENITOGONZALEZSAX</strong>, the exercise of the right of access will depend on the functionality of
            each social network and on the possibilities of access to user profile information. With regard to the rights
            of access and rectification, we recommend that you bear in mind that these can only be fulfilled in relation
            to information under the control of <strong>BENITOGONZALEZSAX</strong>.
          </p>
          <p>
            In addition, you may stop interacting with, following or receiving information from the social media profiles
            of <strong> BENITOGONZALEZSAX</strong>, delete content that no longer interests you or restrict who you share
            your connections with, by using the mechanisms provided in each social network.
          </p>
          <p>
            Users may access the privacy policies of each social network and configure their profile to ensure their
            privacy. <strong>BENITOGONZALEZSAX</strong> encourages users to familiarise themselves with the terms of use
            of the different social networks before starting to use them:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>
              Facebook:
              <a href="https://www.facebook.com/help/323540651073243/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-primary underline">
                Facebook privacy policy
              </a>
            </li>
            <li>
              Google:
              <a href="http://www.google.es/intl/es/policies/privacy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-primary underline">
                Google privacy policy
              </a>
            </li>
            <li>
              Twitter:
              <a href="https://twitter.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-primary underline">
                Twitter privacy policy
              </a>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <h2 class="text-6xl font-segmentA uppercase tracking-wide font-bold mb-4 text-primary">10. Acceptance and consent</h2>
        <p class="mb-4">
          The User declares that they have been informed of the conditions regarding the protection of personal data,
          accepting and consenting to the processing of such data by <strong>BENITOGONZALEZSAX</strong> in the manner and
          for the purposes indicated in this legal notice.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-6xl font-segmentA uppercase tracking-wide font-bold mb-4 text-primary">11. Changes to this Privacy Policy</h2>
        <p class="mb-4">
          <strong>BENITOGONZALEZSAX</strong> reserves the right to modify this policy in order to adapt it to new
          legislative or case law developments, as well as to industry practices. In such cases, the Provider will
          announce the changes on this page with reasonable advance notice of their implementation.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-6xl font-segmentA uppercase tracking-wide font-bold mb-4 text-primary">12. Intellectual property and use of content</h2>
        <div class="flex flex-col gap-4 mb-4">
          <p>
            The general content of the WEBSITE (images, texts, logos) is the property of
            <strong> BENITOGONZALEZSAX</strong>. No content of the WEBSITE may be reproduced, mentioned or linked by any
            technical means without the prior express written permission of <strong>BENITOGONZALEZSAX</strong>.
          </p>
          <p>
            From time to time, this WEBSITE may publish content from other contributors in the form of specialised
            articles or blog posts. In all cases, the reproduction and linking permissions described in this section for
            proprietary content will also apply.
          </p>
        </div>
    </div>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Layout>

<style>
  .prose h2 {
    color: #1a1a1a;
    margin-top: 2rem;
  }
  
  .prose ul {
